{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QHarmonicFlow","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QHarmonicFlow","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.vacuum_stationary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.vacuum_stationary","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-flow.lean#L71-L75","doc":"**The vacuum is a fixed point.** When the configuration is the trivial\n(zero) field, the flow is stationary — the vacuum constant `q ≡ q₀`\nis the trivial `q`-harmonic section. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.stationary_iff_qharmonic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.stationary_iff_qharmonic","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-flow.lean#L64-L69","doc":"**Fixed points are exactly the q-harmonic configurations.** The flow is\nstationary (`∂_t q = 0`) iff the configuration is `q`-harmonic\n(`Δ_q q = 0`). Verified, conditional on the `QHarmonicFlow` class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.flow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.flow","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-flow.lean#L58-L58","doc":"**The ansatz**: the q-harmonic-map heat-flow law `∂_t q = -Δ_q q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.Δq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.Δq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-flow.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The `q`-Laplacian annihilates the zero configuration (it is a\nsecond-order linear differential operator with no zeroth-order\nterm). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.Δq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.Δq","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-flow.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The `q`-Laplacian `Δ_q` acting on field configurations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.dq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.dq","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-flow.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The time-derivative `∂_t q` of the configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.q","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-flow.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The substrate-field configuration `q(p)` (a single time-slice). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-flow.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LocalQ.QHarmonicFlow","kind":"class","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-flow.lean#L38-L58","doc":"**q-harmonic-map heat flow (ANSATZ).** A substrate-field configuration\n`q ∈ V`, its time-derivative `dq = ∂_t q`, and the `q`-Laplacian\n`Δq`, postulated to satisfy the gradient/heat-flow law\n`∂_t q = -Δ_q q`.\n\nThe *existence* of such a structure for the physical substrate field\nis the conjecture (Route 2b Step 3 ansatz); every theorem in this\nnamespace is a verified consequence *conditional on* the class. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:q-harmonic-flow","label":"conj:q-harmonic-flow","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-harmonic-flow.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}